IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-seat-defaults`
IMPORT `je21-part3a-consolidation`
IMPORT `je21-schedule1`
IMPORT `je21-art15-16-revision-publication`
IMPORT `je21-art17-18-official-versions`
IMPORT `je21-part4-office`

-- je21-seat-3-versions-and-publication: the questions a reader of an enactment asks about consolidated, revised and official versions of legislation, about publication, and about privilege in dealing with the Legislative Drafting Office.
-- Each question takes the facts the reader can state and no reading of a fork: it uses the default in je21-seat-defaults.
-- Where a rule module answers FALSE meaning "this Article does not give the effect", and the Law says nothing about the rest, the exported question refuses and says so.
-- None of these questions is asked as at a day: the deposited texts of the Law do not differ in the Articles they rest on.

§ `Articles 12 to 16 -- consolidated and revised legislation, publication`

-- src:121 | (2) As-enacted legislation is legislation containing the text of the legislation as originally made and includes that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under this Part.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 12(2) (src:121)
@export Is this text as-enacted legislation? It is if it contains the text of the legislation as originally made, or is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3.
GIVEN `it contains the text of the legislation as originally made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it contains the text of the legislation as originally made
      `it is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this text as-enacted legislation?` `it contains the text of the legislation as originally made` `it is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3` MEANS
    `Article 12(2): the text is as-enacted legislation` `it contains the text of the legislation as originally made` `it is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3`

-- src:122 | (3) Consolidated legislation is legislation that includes within it any other modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated.
-- src:123 | (4) Revised legislation is also consolidated legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 12(3) and (4) (src:122-123)
@export Is this text consolidated legislation? It is if it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated, and revised legislation is consolidated legislation too.
GIVEN `it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated
      `it is revised legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it is revised legislation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this text consolidated legislation?` `it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated` `it is revised legislation` MEANS
    `Article 12(3) and (4): the text is consolidated legislation` `it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated` `it is revised legislation`

-- src:125 | (1) When any Jersey legislation (other than legislation having the effect only to amend or commence other legislation or consisting of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)) is commenced, amended or revised after the commencement of this Part, the Principal Legislative Drafter must, as soon as practicable, prepare a consolidated version of the legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 13(1) (src:125)
@export Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared? It does when Jersey legislation is commenced, amended or revised after Part 3 of the Law came into force on 28 September 2021, unless it only amends or commences other legislation or is an Act referred to in Article 2(2).
GIVEN `it is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it is Jersey legislation
      `it has the effect only to amend or commence other legislation, or consists of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it has the effect only to amend or commence other legislation, or consists of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)
      event IS AN `Event that calls for a consolidated version` @desc What has happened to the legislation: commenced, amended or revised
      `the day on which the event happened` IS A DATE @desc The day on which that happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` `it is Jersey legislation` `it has the effect only to amend or commence other legislation, or consists of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` event `the day on which the event happened` MEANS
    `Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` `it is Jersey legislation` `it has the effect only to amend or commence other legislation, or consists of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` event `the day on which the event happened` `default reading L3`

-- src:126 | (2) Consolidated legislation must include a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of this Law.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 13(2) (src:126)
@export Does this consolidated legislation carry the statement the Law requires? It must say that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021.
GIVEN `the text is consolidated legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the text is consolidated legislation
      `it includes a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the text includes a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does this consolidated legislation carry the statement the Law requires?` `the text is consolidated legislation` `it includes a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021` MEANS
    `Article 13(2): the consolidated legislation includes the statement the Law requires` `the text is consolidated legislation` `it includes a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021`

-- src:128 | (1) The Principal Legislative Drafter may make the following changes to consolidated legislation (whether when preparing it or later) –
-- src:129 | (a) the removal of a provision relating to its commencement;
-- src:130 | (b) the removal of a provision that amends or repeals other legislation (or any provision of that other legislation);
-- src:131 | (c) the removal of any other provision that the Principal Legislative Drafter considers to be spent or for any other reason to be no longer operative;
-- src:132 | (d) the correction of –
-- src:133 | (i) typographical and clerical errors,
-- src:134 | (ii) errors in grammar, spelling and punctuation,
-- src:135 | (iii) errors in numbering, cross-referencing, and alphabetical ordering,
-- src:136 | (iv) errors in, or arising out of, an amendment by other legislation to the legislation being consolidated, and
-- src:137 | (v) any other errors of a similar nature;
-- src:138 | (e) changes in punctuation and the relocation of conjunctives or disjunctives to enable the addition or removal of any provision that is or was part of a list of provisions.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(1) (src:128-138)
@export May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change to consolidated legislation? Article 14(1) lets the Drafter remove spent provisions and correct errors of the kinds it lists in consolidated legislation.
GIVEN change IS AN `Editorial change under Article 14(1)` @desc The editorial change
      `the text is consolidated legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the text is consolidated legislation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` change `the text is consolidated legislation` MEANS
    IF `Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` change `the text is consolidated legislation`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 14(1) gives the power for consolidated legislation, and the Law does not say whether the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change in any other text"

-- src:139 | (2) However, none of these changes has effect to the extent of changing the meaning of any provision.[3]
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(2) (src:139)
@export Does this editorial change have effect in full? None of the changes under Article 14(1) has effect to the extent of changing the meaning of a provision.
GIVEN `the change would alter the meaning of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the change would alter the meaning of a provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does this editorial change have effect in full?` `the change would alter the meaning of a provision` MEANS
    `Article 14(2): the editorial change has effect in full` `the change would alter the meaning of a provision`

-- src:140 | (3) The Principal Legislative Drafter may make formatting and presentational changes to the legislation so that consolidated legislation is consistent with current drafting practice.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(3) (src:140)
@export May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this formatting or presentational change to consolidated legislation so that it is consistent with current drafting practice?
GIVEN `the text is consolidated legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the text is consolidated legislation
      `the change is made so that the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the change is made so that the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this formatting or presentational change?` `the text is consolidated legislation` `the change is made so that the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice` MEANS
    IF `Article 14(3): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the formatting or presentational change` `the text is consolidated legislation` `the change is made so that the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 14(3) gives the power for formatting and presentational changes to consolidated legislation made so that it is consistent with current drafting practice, and the Law does not say whether the Drafter may make the change otherwise"

-- src:142 | (5) Changes authorised by this Article that are made to consolidated legislation, other than formatting and presentational changes or minor editorial changes, must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(5) (src:142)
@export Must this change authorised by Article 14 be set out in an endnote or other suitable place? It must, other than a formatting or presentational change or a minor editorial change.
GIVEN `it is a formatting or presentational change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it is a formatting or presentational change
      `it is a minor editorial change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it is a minor editorial change
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must this change be set out in an endnote or other suitable place?` `it is a formatting or presentational change` `it is a minor editorial change` MEANS
    `Article 14(5): the change must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place` `it is a formatting or presentational change` `it is a minor editorial change`

-- src:143 | (6) The Principal Legislative Drafter may correct any errors in a published version of as-enacted legislation that occurred after it is made or in revised legislation that occurred after its revision.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(6) (src:143)
@export May the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in a published version? Article 14(6) lets the Drafter correct an error in a published version of as-enacted legislation that occurred after it was made, or of revised legislation that occurred after its revision.
GIVEN version IS A `Published version for Article 14(6)` @desc Which published version has the error
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in a published version?` version MEANS
    IF `Article 14(6): the Principal Legislative Drafter may correct the error` version
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 14(6) lets the Principal Legislative Drafter correct an error in a published version of as-enacted legislation that occurred after it was made, or of revised legislation that occurred after its revision, and the Law does not say whether the Drafter may correct any other"

§ `Article 15 and Schedule 1 -- revision`

-- src:154 | (4) The Principal Legislative Drafter may prepare in draft a revision of any Jersey legislation in accordance with any of the powers set out in Schedule 1.
-- src:155 | (5) The powers in Article 14 may also be used for the preparation of the revision.
-- src:227 | In preparing a revision under Article 15 the Law Revision Board has the power –
-- src:228 | (a) to amend the citation provision, long title, short title, words of enactment or preamble of any legislation;
-- src:229 | (b) to consolidate or split any legislation or relocate a provision into different legislation where the provision more properly belongs;
-- src:230 | (c) to rearrange the provisions of any legislation or any list in a provision of any legislation;
-- src:231 | (d) to add a table of contents or destinations to any legislation;
-- src:232 | (e) to add a heading to a provision of any legislation that does not have one and alter any heading to a provision or part of any legislation;
-- src:233 | (f) to omit any map, picture, drawing, diagram or other object;
-- src:234 | (g) to change any reference to a person, office, body, place or thing to reflect a change of name, transfer of function or provision for construction of the reference;
-- src:235 | (h) to make any adaptations and amendments that may appear necessary or proper as a consequence of constitutional or other changes in Jersey or any other place or territory or in or to any body or organisation outside Jersey;
-- src:236 | (i) to change any words to make them gender neutral;
-- src:237 | (j) to change expressions of date, money, number, time and units of measurement;
-- src:238 | (k) to delete any obsolete or redundant words or provisions;
-- src:239 | (l) to alter any words to secure uniformity of expression in any legislation;
-- src:240 | (m) to shorten any phrase or sentence;
-- src:241 | (n) to change the wording for the better application of plain language principles;
-- src:242 | (o) to add numbering to or renumber any provision;
-- src:243 | (p) to substitute for a reference to any legislation or provision of any legislation that has been re-enacted or replaced, whether with or without modifications, a reference to the legislation or provision re-enacting or replacing it; and
-- src:244 | (q) to do all other things that appear to the Board to be necessary to render revised legislation consistent with current drafting practice.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(4) and (5) and Schedule 1 (src:154-155, src:227-244)
@export Is the power relied on for this change one that Schedule 1 or Article 14 gives the Law Revision Board?
GIVEN authority IS AN `Authority relied on for a change` @desc The power the statement relies on for the change: a paragraph of Schedule 1, an editorial change of Article 14(1), or none
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the power relied on for this change one the Law gives?` authority MEANS
    `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` authority

-- src:156 | (6) The Principal Legislative Drafter must submit the draft revision to the other members of the Law Revision Board accompanied by a statement setting out the changes made (other than editorial changes) and the power relied on as authority for the change.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(6) (src:156)
@export Does the statement accompanying the draft revision name a power for every change? Article 15(6) requires the statement to set out the changes made and the power relied on as authority for each.
GIVEN changes IS A LIST OF `Change in a draft revision` @desc The changes in the draft revision other than editorial changes, each with the power relied on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does the statement name a power for every change?` changes MEANS
    `Article 15(6): the statement names a power for every change` changes

-- src:157 | (7) The Law Revision Board may certify the draft revision as revised legislation only if it is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(7) (src:157)
@export Are all the changes in this draft revision within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1? An empty draft has all its changes within the powers.
GIVEN changes IS A LIST OF `Change in a draft revision` @desc The changes in the draft revision other than editorial changes, each with the power relied on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Are all the changes in this draft revision within the powers of Article 14 or Schedule 1?` changes MEANS
    `Article 15(7): all the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` changes

-- src:157 | (7) The Law Revision Board may certify the draft revision as revised legislation only if it is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(7) (src:157)
@export May the Law Revision Board certify the draft revision as revised legislation? It may only if it is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1.
GIVEN `the Board is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Law Revision Board is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May the Law Revision Board certify the draft revision as revised legislation?` `the Board is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` MEANS
    `Article 15(7): certification is open to the Board` `the Board is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1`

-- src:158 | (8) The changes made to legislation by a revision have effect as if they were effected by an amendment made by other legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(8) (src:158)
@export Do the changes made by a revision have effect as if they were made by an amendment in other legislation? They do for a revision certified under Article 15(7).
GIVEN `the draft revision has been certified as revised legislation under Article 15(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the draft revision has been certified as revised legislation under Article 15(7)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do the changes made by a revision have effect as if made by an amendment in other legislation?` `the draft revision has been certified as revised legislation under Article 15(7)` MEANS
    `Article 15(8): the changes made by the revision have effect as if effected by an amendment made by other legislation` `the draft revision has been certified as revised legislation under Article 15(7)`

-- src:159 | (9) The Minutes or other record of the transactions of the business of the Law Revision Board must be laid before the States within 2 months of the business being transacted.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(9) (src:159)
@export Did the Law Revision Board lay its minutes before the States in time? They must be laid within 2 months of the business being transacted; the last permitted day is given, and the minutes laid on that day are in time.
GIVEN `the day on which the minutes were laid before the States` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Law Revision Board's minutes were laid before the States
      `the last day on which they could be laid within 2 months of the business being transacted` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which the minutes could be laid within 2 months of the business being transacted, worked out under the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Did the Board lay its minutes before the States in time?` `the day on which the minutes were laid before the States` `the last day on which they could be laid within 2 months of the business being transacted` MEANS
    `Article 15(9): the minutes were laid in time` `the day on which the minutes were laid before the States` `the last day on which they could be laid within 2 months of the business being transacted`

§ `Article 16 -- publication`

-- src:162 | (1) The Principal Legislative Drafter must ensure that the following are published –
-- src:163 | (a) all as-enacted legislation made after the commencement of this Part;
-- src:164 | (b) all consolidated legislation prepared after 1st January 2019.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 16(1) (src:162-164)
@export Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published? The Principal Legislative Drafter must ensure that all as-enacted legislation made after Part 3 of the Law came into force on 28 September 2021 is published, and all consolidated legislation prepared after 1 January 2019.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of text under Part 3` @desc Whether the legislation is as-enacted, consolidated or revised legislation
      `the day on which it was made or prepared` IS A DATE @desc The day an as-enacted text was made, or a consolidated or revised text was prepared
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` kind `the day on which it was made or prepared` MEANS
    `Article 16(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must ensure that the legislation is published` kind `the day on which it was made or prepared` `default reading L3`

-- src:165 | (2) As-enacted legislation must be published as soon as practicable after it is made and consolidated legislation must be published as soon as practicable after it is consolidated or the amendments resulting from other legislation are incorporated within it, whichever is the later.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 16(2) (src:165)
@export From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable? As-enacted legislation, from the day it is made; consolidated legislation, from the later of the day it is consolidated and the day the amendments are incorporated. What is practicable is a judgement, and no deadline is computed.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of text under Part 3` @desc Whether the legislation is as-enacted, consolidated or revised legislation
      `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated` IS A DATE @desc The day an as-enacted text was made, or a consolidated or revised text was consolidated
      `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated` IS A DATE @desc The day the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated in a consolidated text; not used for as-enacted legislation
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` kind `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated` `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated` MEANS
    `Article 16(2): the day from which publication is due as soon as practicable` kind `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated` `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated`

§ `Articles 17 and 18 -- official versions, Statute Law Revision Regulations`

-- src:167 | (1) All as-enacted legislation is an official version of the legislation.
-- src:168 | (2) Any consolidated legislation that is Jersey legislation is an official version if it contains a statement that it is an official version of the legislation issued under the authority of this Law and –
-- src:169 | (a) it is an electronic version of the legislation displayed on a website under the authority of the Principal Legislative Drafter (or a printed or downloaded version of that legislation without any alteration to its text or format); or
-- src:170 | (b) it is a printed version of the legislation issued by or on behalf of the Principal Legislative Drafter.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(1) and (2) (src:167-170)
@export Is this text an official version of the legislation? All as-enacted legislation is. Consolidated legislation that is Jersey legislation is if it carries the statement that it is an official version issued under the authority of the Law, and is either the electronic version displayed on a website under the authority of the Principal Legislative Drafter (or an unaltered printed or downloaded copy) or a printed version issued by or for the Drafter.
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text` @desc The facts about the text: its kind, whether it is Jersey legislation, whether it carries the statement that it is an official version, and how it was issued
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this text an official version of the legislation?` text MEANS
    `Article 17(1) and (2): the text is an official version` text `default reading L11`

-- src:171 | (3) An official version of as-enacted legislation is taken to set out correctly the text of the legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(3) (src:171)
@export Is the official version of this as-enacted legislation taken to set out its text correctly? It is, and the Law gives no way to show the contrary.
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text` @desc The facts about the text: its kind, whether it is Jersey legislation, whether it carries the statement that it is an official version, and how it was issued
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the official version taken to set out the text of the as-enacted legislation correctly?` text MEANS
    `Article 17(3): the official version is taken to set out the text of the as-enacted legislation correctly` text

-- src:172 | (4) Subject to Article 15(8) (changes made by revision have effect as if effected by amendment), an official version of consolidated legislation, unless the contrary is shown, is taken to set out correctly, as at the date on which it is stated to be consolidated, the legislation as enacted and including any current amendments to it, or revisions of it.[4]
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(4) (src:172)
@export Is the official version of this consolidated legislation taken to set out the legislation correctly as at the date it is stated to be consolidated? It is, unless the contrary is shown.
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text` @desc The facts about the text: its kind, whether it is Jersey legislation, whether it carries the statement that it is an official version, and how it was issued
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it is shown that the official version does not set the legislation out correctly
      `the question is about the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if you are asking about the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` text `the contrary is shown` `the question is about the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated` MEANS
    `Article 17(4): the official version is taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly` text `the contrary is shown` `the question is about the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated`

-- src:173 | (5) An official version of legislation is admissible in evidence in any proceedings and a court or person acting judicially must take judicial notice of any official version of legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(5) (src:173)
@export Is this text admissible in evidence in any proceedings? An official version of legislation is.
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text` @desc The facts about the text: its kind, whether it is Jersey legislation, whether it carries the statement that it is an official version, and how it was issued
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this text admissible in evidence?` text MEANS
    `Article 17(5): the text is admissible in evidence in any proceedings` text

-- src:173 | (5) An official version of legislation is admissible in evidence in any proceedings and a court or person acting judicially must take judicial notice of any official version of legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(5) (src:173)
@export Must a court or person acting judicially take judicial notice of this text? Of any official version of legislation, it must.
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text` @desc The facts about the text: its kind, whether it is Jersey legislation, whether it carries the statement that it is an official version, and how it was issued
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must a court take judicial notice of this text?` text MEANS
    `Article 17(5): a court or person acting judicially must take judicial notice of the text` text

-- src:176 | (1) The States may by Regulations amend any Jersey legislation using the powers set out in paragraph (2), Article 14 or Schedule 1.
-- src:177 | (2) The power is to make such amendments as are necessary or desirable to –
-- src:178 | (a) clarify any ambiguity in the legislation; or
-- src:179 | (b) reconcile inconsistencies between different provisions of the legislation or between any of its provisions and provisions of any other Jersey legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 18(1) and (2) (src:176-179)
@export Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment? The States may by Regulations amend any Jersey legislation to clarify an ambiguity or reconcile inconsistencies, or using a power in Article 14 or Schedule 1.
GIVEN `the legislation to be amended is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation to be amended is Jersey legislation
      ground IS A `Ground of an amendment under Article 18` @desc What the amendment rests on: clarifying an ambiguity, reconciling inconsistencies, a power in Article 14, a power in Schedule 1, or none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` `the legislation to be amended is Jersey legislation` ground MEANS
    `Article 18(1) and (2): Statute Law Revision Regulations may make the amendment` `the legislation to be amended is Jersey legislation` ground

-- src:180 | (3) Where a proposition is lodged in respect of Regulations to be made under this Article no amendment may be lodged that, in the opinion of the Bailiff, would alter the effect of any legislation unless it is within the scope of paragraphs (1) or (2).
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 18(3) (src:180)
@export Is this amendment to a proposition for Statute Law Revision Regulations not barred from being lodged? No amendment may be lodged that in the opinion of the Bailiff would alter the effect of any legislation unless it is within the scope of Article 18(1) or (2).
GIVEN `the proposition is for Regulations to be made under Article 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the proposition lodged is for Regulations to be made under Article 18
      `in the opinion of the Bailiff the amendment would alter the effect of legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if in the opinion of the Bailiff the amendment would alter the effect of any legislation
      `the legislation the amendment would amend is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation the amendment would amend is Jersey legislation
      ground IS A `Ground of an amendment under Article 18` @desc What the amendment rests on: clarifying an ambiguity, reconciling inconsistencies, a power in Article 14, a power in Schedule 1, or none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` `the proposition is for Regulations to be made under Article 18` `in the opinion of the Bailiff the amendment would alter the effect of legislation` `the legislation the amendment would amend is Jersey legislation` ground MEANS
    `Article 18(3): the amendment is not barred from being lodged` `the proposition is for Regulations to be made under Article 18` `in the opinion of the Bailiff the amendment would alter the effect of legislation` `the legislation the amendment would amend is Jersey legislation` ground

-- src:181 | (4) Subject to this Article, the Regulations may make any provision that could be made by a Law.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 18(4) (src:181)
@export May Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision? Subject to Article 18, they may make any provision that could be made by a Law.
GIVEN `a Law could make the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if a Law could make the provision
      `any amendment the provision makes is one Article 18(1) and (2) give the power to make` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if any amendment the provision makes is one Article 18(1) and (2) give the power to make
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision?` `a Law could make the provision` `any amendment the provision makes is one Article 18(1) and (2) give the power to make` MEANS
    `Article 18(4): Statute Law Revision Regulations may make the provision` `a Law could make the provision` `any amendment the provision makes is one Article 18(1) and (2) give the power to make`

§ `Article 22 -- privilege`

-- src:208 | (1) Confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter are subject to legal professional privilege.
-- src:209 | (2) In this Article –
-- src:210 | “confidential communications” includes –
-- src:211 | (a) instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office and communications between any client of the Legislative Drafting Office and any Legislative Drafter that relate to the subject matter of the instructions;
-- src:212 | (b) unpublished drafts of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the Legislative Drafting Office;
-- src:213 | “provider of instructions” includes a Member of the States and any officer working in –
-- src:214 | (a) a department established by the States; or
-- src:215 | (b) a body, office or unit of administration, established on behalf of the States (including under any legislation).
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 22 (src:208-215)
@export Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office subject to legal professional privilege? Confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Office and a Legislative Drafter are.
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a provider of instructions` @desc The facts about the person who gave or gives instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office
      `the other party's role` IS A `Role in the Legislative Drafting Office` @desc The role in the Legislative Drafting Office of the other party to the communication
      kind IS A `Kind of communication under Article 22` @desc What kind of communication it is
      `the communication is confidential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the communication is confidential; instructions, client communications and unpublished drafts count whatever you say
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` person `the other party's role` kind `the communication is confidential` MEANS
    IF `Article 22(1): the communication is subject to legal professional privilege` person `the other party's role` kind `the communication is confidential`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 22 gives legal professional privilege to confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter, and the Law says nothing of other communications"

